style suggestion: do not rely on the DO variable 'a' after the loop
  --> tests/../integration_tests/common_05.f90:34:14
   |
34 |     print *, a, b, c, d
   |              ^ after the loop, 'a' is one step past the last iteration
   |
31 |     do a = 1, c(1), 1
   |        ~ the loop sets 'a' here
   = help: the value is well defined, but it depends on how the loop ends and
           is easy to misread; inside the loop, assign the value you need to
           a variable with a meaningful name instead
